    "highlights": "Heavy use of CSS compositing for typography, including `<feTurbulence>` noise filters applied as background-image clippings on text, mix-blend-modes (mix-blend-plus-lighter), and duplicate layered DOM text elements with varying `blur()` radii to create glowing, \"soft focus\" typographic halos. Extreme tight tracking is applied to large display text (`tracking-[-1.1px]`, `tracking-[-0.04em]`). Almost all UI components and display headings force `uppercase`.",
    "insights": [
      "Distinct Typographic Roles: The system clearly divides typography into 'font-display' (Archivo) for large, tight-tracked, emotional messaging, and 'font-ui' (Archivo Narrow) for sharp, uppercase navigation, buttons, and technical tags.",
      "Experimental Rendering Techniques: Ghost.ai uses techniques usually reserved for images—like SVG noise filters applied via background-image, backdrop-filters, and multi-layered blurred DOM elements—to create rich, atmospheric text treatments directly in CSS.",
      "Aggressive Fluidity & Tight Fitting: There is heavy reliance on fluid `clamp()` values and extreme negative letter-spacing for large text, ensuring that the brand’s technical aesthetic is maintained perfectly across diverse viewport sizes."
    ]
